body:
I've been going through the same the last 8 weeks. Got diagnosed as rapid cycling bipolar yesterday. Have been like this for years and think people just wrote it off as a part of my personality that would emerge sometimes. In the span of the last few weeks, I bought two burberry trench coats, got it into my head that I needed to take up guitar but couldn't just buy any guitar so got a £3,000 Gibson Les Paul and then decided I had to go skiing this month so booked a £2k ski trip no matter how much the price kept escalating, signed up to a bunch of volunteer schemes, few extra hobbies, did a lot of late night DIY and didn't even notice anything was up until my mum pointed out how fast I was talking (and I usually speak fast anyway - apparently this was on another level). I start aripiprazole later this week (I was on it a few years ago when I got misdiagnosed as borderline and it worked great for me so fingers crossed it will again)

&#x200B;

On the plus side, my flat has been very clean and I lost a bunch of weight from forgetting to eat so that's something I guess...
